{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>And I will shut up.</b> Some interchange the kaf with gimel, but in truth only the similar and correct letters interchange, for it is from the same root as ויסכרו מעינות תהום (Genesis 1:2)." "<b>A harsh master.</b> Its grammar is explained in the Torah (Exodus 21:4)." "<b>And a mighty king.</b> He is the king of Assyria."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:54:15.076089340Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}